 "teaches": [
  "Points as data: {\"label\": \"La Paz\", \"x\": 472, \"y\": 0.76, \"z\": 3640, \"size\": 0.76}; the server maps them into the box (x 0..3000, y 0..20, z 0..4000) and sizes spheres by area",
  "One sphere mesh drawn in a loop per colour step over a float array of positions and radii: 18 points cost 18 floats x 6, not 18 meshes",
  "Stems to the floor show where each point stands and how high; the three highest named points get labels with a halo",
  "fill: true in a box with verticalWeight 1: the chart takes the remaining height, and the camera reframes for any aspect"
 ],
